  {"name":"Sae","aliases":[],"role":"Neo-Haven workshop contact; stabilizer lattice supplier","bio":'''Middle-aged, practical, call-stained fingers; runs a copper-weave mute room in the Crimson Market. Cleaned the stabilizer lattice with no Board tags. Confessed to Naobito Yagami in high school and stayed behind selling sealed work while he became a rumor with casualties. Gives Kitsuke the advice not to answer soft things with silence.''',"first_appearance_context":'''Stepping out from behind the canvas partition in the dampened workshop.'''},
  {"name":"Naobito Yagami","aliases":["Great Naobito Yagami","the Yagami boy","the quiet boy who fixed other people's problems"],"role":"Legendary Yagami; Haruto's father (referenced)","bio":'''Haruto's father and the subject of compound rumor: a man who stepped into powers older systems preferred caged, partnered with others, fought in the Dome tournament, and left behind names like Queen, Keys, and Board. Remembered by Sae as an introvert who rejected her kindly, then became "a rumor with casualties." His direction matters to Haruto's blood even when Haruto chooses a different road.''',"first_appearance_context":'''First heard as a name in the east linen room when two maids whisper about "the Yagami boy, not this one. The father. Naobito."'''},
  {"name":"Kenshi Kashimo","aliases":["uncle Kenshi"],"role":"Kei's uncle; unbound speed talent (referenced)","bio":'''Smug on purpose, useful against his will, and unbound in a way that makes institutions nervous and survivors loyal. Elder Saito describes him as a personality that happens to move too fast; Haruto respects him as unconditionally caring, smart, and unbound. His Kashimo routes reach places Kurogane banners do not.''',"first_appearance_context":'''First named by Kei as her uncle; then recalled from Elder Saito's childhood corridor complaint about outside talents.'''},
  {"name":"Suspicious Elder","aliases":["polished-wood elder"],"role":"Manipulative clan elder; offers Kitsuke an alternate cage","bio":'''Smooth, kindly seeming, and rehearsed. Approaches Kitsuke near the east records annex, warns him that some clan attention is inventory not protection, and offers "a place better than this compound" whenever Kitsuke feels finished with. His gentleness reads as a door closing.''',"first_appearance_context":'''Already in Kitsuke's path when he turns from watching the courier and the elder at the east records annex.'''},
